cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the software release and the paper below."
title: "GSPICE: GausSian PIxelwise Conditional Estimation"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/dfink/gspice"
abstract: >-
  GSPICE models an ensemble of spectra as a multivariate Gaussian and estimates
  the expected value and variance of each pixel of each spectrum conditional on
  other pixels. Comparing observed fluxes with these estimates identifies
  outliers such as cosmic rays and wavelength-calibration errors, which can be
  masked or replaced by their estimates. This release contains the Python,
  IDL and Julia implementations, and Python routines for repair of masked
  pixels, blockwise prediction and transformation back to flux units.
keywords:
  - spectra
  - Gaussian process
  - conditional estimation
  - outlier detection
  - astronomy
